# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your own key.
# `.env.local` is git-ignored, so your key never leaves your machine.
#
# Get a free key at https://unsplash.com/developers (register an app, then
# copy the "Access Key" — NOT the Secret Key).
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with `VITE_` to the browser.
# Note: because this app has no backend, this key IS visible in the built
# JS bundle. That's fine for a personal homepage you host yourself, but
# don't publish the build somewhere public with a key you care about.
#
# If you leave this blank, the app quietly falls back to the small set of
# gradient backgrounds bundled in `src/assets/backgrounds/`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: accounts and cloud sync via Supabase. Leave both blank to use the
# app entirely offline with localStorage, same as always — the sign-in
# button in the header simply doesn't appear.
#
# 1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com.
# 2. Run the SQL in README.md's "Adding accounts" section in the project's
#    SQL editor — it creates the table these two values let the app read
#    and write, scoped to each signed-in user.
# 3. Project Settings -> API for the URL and the anon/public key.
#
# The anon key is safe to expose in client code by design — it identifies
# the project, not a user. What actually protects each user's data is the
# Row Level Security policy from that SQL, not secrecy of this key. Same
# "safe to ship, no backend needed" reasoning as the Unsplash key above.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: sync to the user's OWN cloud storage instead of a backend you run.
# Leave blank and the provider simply isn't offered in Settings -> Sync.
#
# Unlike the Supabase option above, nothing here costs you anything at any
# scale: each person's bookmarks live in their own Dropbox, under their own
# quota, in a folder this app can't see outside of.
#
# Dropbox: create an app at https://www.dropbox.com/developers/apps
#   - Access type: "App folder" (NOT "Full Dropbox" — the whole point is that
#     this app can only ever touch its own folder)
#   - Permissions tab: account_info.read, files.content.read, files.content.write
#   - Settings tab -> Redirect URIs: add "<your origin>/oauth-callback.html"
#     for every origin you use, including http://localhost:5173 for dev
#   - Copy the "App key" below. There is no secret to copy: the browser uses
#     PKCE, which is exactly what lets this work with no backend.
#
# Heads up before you invite anyone: a Dropbox app stays in development mode
# until you apply for production, which caps it at ~50 linked accounts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_DROPBOX_APP_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Drive: create an OAuth client at https://console.cloud.google.com
#   - Enable the Google Drive API for the project
#   - Credentials -> Create OAuth client ID -> Web application
#   - Authorised JavaScript origins: every origin you use, including
#     http://localhost:5173 for dev
#   - Copy the "Client ID" below. The client secret is NOT used and must not
#     be put in here: this app uses Google Identity Services' token flow from
#     the browser precisely because a secret can't live in a JS bundle.
#   - OAuth consent screen: add the scope
#     https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.appdata
#
# That scope reaches a hidden per-app folder and nothing else in anyone's
# Drive. It is still classed as sensitive, so an unverified app is limited to
# the test users you list — fine for yourself and friends, but going public
# means Google's verification process.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
